Remove the extra colon after the authority in hyperlinks. It was introduced in
2.3.0 and produces invalid file://hostname:/path URLs.

Upstream acknowledged the issue and plans this removal for the next release:
https://github.com/Old-Man-Programmer/tree/issues/64

--- a/unix.c
+++ b/unix.c
@@ -46,7 +46,6 @@ void open_hyperlink(char *dirname, char *filename)
 {
   fprintf(outfile,"\033]8;;%s", scheme);
   url_encode(outfile, authority);
-  fprintf(outfile, ":");
   // (optional) Hanging slashes are a real pain to deal with
   bool slash = url_encode(outfile, realbasepath);
   if (*(dirname+dirpathoffset)) {
